<InformationLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="How Elementa keeps study data in your browser, measures website usage, and handles optional external video and reference links.">
  <p>Last updated November 11, 2026.</p>
  <h2>Study data stored on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Elementa requires no student account, name, email address, birth date or school.
    Your saved elements, mastery marks, notes and quiz history are stored in this
    browser on this device. The study app doesn't upload this progress to a cloud
    profile. Website analytics are separate from your study records.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use <a href="/study/#/saved">Export JSON on the Saved page</a> to keep a backup
    or move progress to another browser. Importing a backup is an action you choose.
    Remove individual saved items in the app, or clear this site's data in your
    browser settings to remove local progress. Smolk Apps can't recover cleared
    browser data.
  </p>
  <h2>Website analytics and delivery</h2>
  <p>
    The reference website uses Umami to measure page visits, referrals and actions
    such as opening an element or starting practice. The website is delivered
    through Cloudflare, which also supplies security and performance measurement.
    These services receive technical information needed for web requests, such as
    the requested URL, IP address and browser information. This site therefore
    shouldn't be treated as a website with no analytics or third-party requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    Study notes, saved decks and quiz-answer records aren't included in the
    website's configured usage events. For more information about these services,
    see <a href="https://umami.is/privacy">Umami's privacy information</a> and
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>
  <h2>Optional video and outside links</h2>
  <p>
    Playing the credited video on the homepage loads media from X/Twitter.
    That provider receives the media requests and applies its own policies.
    The video isn't required to use Elementa. Following a science reference,
    source-code or creator link takes you to another website with its own privacy
    policy.
  </p>
  <h2>Classroom use and questions</h2>
  <p>
    Teachers and students can use the public tools without creating accounts.
    This page doesn't claim certification under a school privacy standard; check
    your school's requirements before classroom use. For questions, email
    <a href="mailto:michael@smolkin.org">michael@smolkin.org</a>.
  </p>
</InformationLayout>
